Entries for the South Dakota QSO Party used by in-state (South Dakota) stations
The 66 South Dakota counties (each its own multiplier), the 50 states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier, not entries here.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before s50.dom (the rules count US States; DC is no state -- a decision recorded in uContestSouthDakotaQP).
SD stays on the list from s50.dom: the rules name US States and DXLog accepts SD (a question for NY4I in issue 129).
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.
https://pdarc.org/sd-qso-party

INCLUDE FILE southdakota_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
